TEXT 8 -432 Left 2 ;50 mOhm max contact resistance for JST GH connectors\n \n5.57 mOhm per inch of 26 AWG aluminum wire\n22.28 mOhm for 4 inches of cable\n \nTPS731 equivalent resistance calculated at change in voltage (ideal Vin = 4.7 V, ideal Vout = 3.3 V, ideal delta V = 1.4 V) divided by typical max output current (360 mA), 1.4 V/ 360 mA = 3.89 Ohm\nRemaining components driven by 3.3 V rail are reduced to an equivalent resistance calculated by 3.3 V / 360 mA = 9.17 Ohm\n \nPCA9615 equivalent resistance calculated at ideal Vin (4.7 V) divided by approximate input current (1 m A) = 4.7 kOhm\n \n50 mOhm max contact resistance for mezzanine connectors, connectors are in parallel = 25 mOhm\n \nColor sensor LED equivalent resistance calculated as operating voltage (2.9 V) divided by operating current (8 mA) = 362.5 Ohm\nAdd with two 120 Ohm resistors in series = 602.5 Ohm\nTwo same branch of series LEDs and resistors in a parallel configuration = 301.25 Ohm
